.TH "RAPTOR-ANALYTIC" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-analytic \- Solve the static subset of an RBD exactly: series, parallel, mixed, k\-out\-of\-n and hierarchies. Reliability mode is non\-repairable. Availability mode is steady state, independent components, perfect repair. Models outside that subset are refused with the first offending element.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor analytic\fR [\-h] [\-\-mode {reliability,availability}] [\-\-at T] [\-\-times T1,T2,...] [\-\-bx X1,X2,...] [\-\-tau T] [\-\-importance] [\-\-no\-importance] [\-\-equation] [\-\-ignore\-repairs] [\-f {text,json,csv}] MODEL
.SH DESCRIPTION
Solve the static subset of an RBD exactly: series, parallel, mixed, k\-out\-of\-n and hierarchies. Reliability mode is non\-repairable. Availability mode is steady state, independent components, perfect repair. Models outside that subset are refused with the first offending element.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI{reliability|availability}\fR
reliability (R(t), non\-repairable) or availability (steady state, repairable) (default reliability)
.TP
\fB\-\-at\fR \fIT\fR
mission time for reliability mode (default: the model's run length); ignored in availability mode
.TP
\fB\-\-times\fR \fIT1,T2,...\fR
also evaluate a curve at these times
.TP
\fB\-\-bx\fR \fIX1,X2,...\fR
BX life percentages for reliability mode (default 10); ignored in availability mode
.TP
\fB\-\-tau\fR \fIT\fR
conditional reliability for another mission of T after \-\-at
.TP
\fB\-\-importance\fR
exact Birnbaum/RAW/RRW/VF/criticality (default on)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-importance\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-equation\fR
print the path\-product equation
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-repairs\fR
reliability mode only: compute first\-failure reliability even when the model has repair distributions
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json|csv}\fR

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
